AU  - Pamidipati Karthik Chandrasekhar
AU  - Patel Hiren
AU  - Bergman Brandon K
JO  - Diabetes care
PY  - 2026
DO  - 10.2337/dc26-1647
AB  - To assess the effect of tirzepatide on kidney parameters in youth-onset type 2 diabetes. In this SURPASS-PEDS analysis, estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) and albuminuria were assessed in 99 participants (aged 10 to <18 years) treated with tirzepatide or placebo. At baseline, 18% of participants exhibited hyperfiltration (mean eGFR 142 vs. 104 mL/min/1.73 m2 in normofiltration), and 26% had a urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio ≥30 mg/g. Tirzepatide (pooled) reduced eGFR, with more than twofold greater reductions in participants with baseline hyperfiltration versus normofiltration at week 30 (-20.2 vs. -8.4 mL/min/1.73 m2; both P < 0.05 vs. placebo). The proportion of participants with hyperfiltration decreased with tirzepatide and increased with placebo (P < 0.05 for pooled tirzepatide vs. placebo). At week 30, fewer participants had albuminuria across all treatment groups. Tirzepatide decreased eGFR in youth with type 2 diabetes and normal to elevated eGFR, an effect primarily ascribed to the attenuation of glomerular hyperfiltration.
UR  - https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/43070923/
